Lepton: time each copy-back step (LEPTON_VA_TIMING)

At the end of a decoding session, log the average wall time per output
frame of each step: avcodec_send_packet, avcodec_receive_frame, the
download (GPU wait plus map or copy), fetching and mapping the output
block, the swscale conversion, and Codec2's whole process() call, with
the session's output frame rate. No behaviour change; a few clock reads
per frame.

diff --git a/codec2/C2FFMPEGVideoDecodeComponent.cpp b/codec2/C2FFMPEGVideoDecodeComponent.cpp
index ddf019e..6881ccb 100644
--- a/codec2/C2FFMPEGVideoDecodeComponent.cpp
+++ b/codec2/C2FFMPEGVideoDecodeComponent.cpp
@@ -255,6 +255,22 @@ c2_status_t C2FFMPEGVideoDecodeComponent::openDecoder() {
     return C2_OK;
 }
 
+// Lepton: wall time of one step, added to a LEPTON_VA_TIMING counter.
+static int64_t leptonNowUs() {
+    struct timespec ts;
+    clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);
+    return (int64_t)ts.tv_sec * 1000000 + ts.tv_nsec / 1000;
+}
+
+namespace {
+struct ScopedStepTime {
+    explicit ScopedStepTime(int64_t& total) : mTotal(total), mStart(leptonNowUs()) {}
+    ~ScopedStepTime() { mTotal += leptonNowUs() - mStart; }
+    int64_t& mTotal;
+    int64_t mStart;
+};
+}  // namespace
+
 // Lepton: one line when a session's first frame arrives, saying whether
 // frames come from VA-API or FFmpeg decodes in software, and why.
